{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine","id":859682,"title":"What is a simple machine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-05T09:11:53-07:00","id":859682,"title":"What is a simple machine?","content":"In the context of this gift, what is the definition of Simple Machine?<br /> Is it any machine without electronics?<br /> Is it the trigger of a gun?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Control Simple Machine (Level One) \u2014 The<br /> Garou may command the spirits of the simplest machines,<br /> causing levers to flip, doors to unbolt, pulleys to roll, and<br /> so on. Any technological spirit can teach this Gift.<br /> System: The player spends a Willpower point and<br /> rolls Manipulation + Crafts (difficulty 7). The Garou\u2019s<br /> control lasts until the end of the scene. </div> </div> </div>Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:39:41-07:00","id":859700,"title":"","content":"It's any simple mechanical system. The trigger of a gun, a deadbolt, clockwork, crane release. I usually go by saying that anything involving chemicals or electronics is beyond the gift. So for instance you could jam the gun by disabling the firing pin, but you couldn't disable it by stopping the gunpowder from igniting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/842395-why-are-open-seal-and-various-stealth-gifts-not-redundant-with-step-sideways\">We've actually had a recent discussion on the topic and one of the devs actually pitched in...</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T09:45:23-07:00","id":859706,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with the gift (the one we most often argue about in our LARP) is: &quot;Does a part of an mechanism constitute an smaller mechanism&quot;. Because, even a computer is simple, if you control each keystroke separately. Sure, the gift costs Willpower, but 'kill all' just needs 6 keys (and hence six willpower) to work. And the trigger of a gun, or the magazine release of an enemy' gun are all pretty simple, too.<br /> <br /> But, strictly by the wording, the trigger of a gun, is akin to a lever and is affected by the gift, so the gun will fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:09:14-07:00","id":859801,"title":"","content":"We usually go by the classical definition of a simple machine (there is such a thing...) where activating the Gift allows you to operate a single function of a single classical simple machine; including the components of more complex machines (since otherwise the Gift is exceedingly weak since very few items are just one simple machine). Though wedges and inclined planes are rarely used since they are about modifying the exertion of force over converting the kind of force in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T00:48:37-07:00","id":860163,"title":"","content":"You use the classical definition which you can find on Wikipedia. A simple machine is a device that changes the direction or magnitude of a force. Generally this is done by leverage alone. The six classical &quot;simple machines&quot; are:<br /> <br /> Lever<br /> Wheel and Axle<br /> Pulley<br /> Incline Plane<br /> Wedge<br /> Screw<br /> <br /> We are talking machines that were known in the Medieval or earlier levels. Almost anything invented in the 19th century or later does not count.<br /> <br /> I personally would not classify any device which has its own power source (gas, electricity, steam), or multiple parts/gears. I might allow a very simple gun (like a revolver), but not anything more complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T01:17:40-07:00","id":860165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine?p=860163#post860163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost anything invented in the 19th century or later does not count.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some pretty significant exceptions to that. Especially if you allow a bit of leeway like the cotton gin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally would not classify any device which has its own power source (gas, electricity, steam), or multiple parts/gears. I might allow a very simple gun (like a revolver), but not anything more complex. </div> </div> </div>I feel that's why it's important to allow it to be used on components. The trigger on a gun is just a lever, just like flipping a light-switch, and what happens when you flip the lever is beyond the control of the Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T02:18:31-07:00","id":860188,"title":"","content":"Let me try and argue against the gift affecting guns.<br /> <br /> By the description, it doesn't affect the physical object--it affects the spirit of the object, and that spirit causes the object to do something. &quot;Pulleys to roll&quot;... You're not moving rope, the Gift doesn't apply leverage to anything; you're asking one of a _narrow_ set of spirits to do you a favor and then that spirit causes the desired thing to happen. In fact, you could probably make a case that pulleys, levers, and doors are all inhabited by the same kind of interchangeable simple-machine-spirit, whatever you want to call that kind of spirit, and those spirits as a class understand how basic physics work. This gift talks to that type of spirit, and those spirits are not found in more complex machines, so you can't talk to them.<br /> <br /> A gun's trigger is very simple, but the gun does not have a barrel-spirit, sight-spirit, trigger-spirit, or a magazine-release-spirit. You're talking to a gun-spirit, and if the ST's discretion is that the gun isn't a &quot;simple machine&quot;, then that's not a spirit you can affect. I think the distinction of revolver vs. other guns is meaningful (though I could imagine an ST going either direction on them).<br /> <br /> Same with typing on a keyboard...the &quot;K&quot; key doesn't have a spirit, you certainly couldn't spend willpower per-key to type stuff. If you used a gift to type something, then you're instead asking the spirit of the keyboard to write something for you, and the spirit will probably just send those characters through the USB cable unless it feels like being flashy. (The distinction between a spirit of your computer-as-a-whole vs. a spirit of your keyboard makes my head hurt, though. Probably I'd assume the keyboard doesn't have a spirit distinct from the computer itself, so you'd really just ask the computer to type something, and it would happen in a way that may not involve the keyboard at all.)<br /> <br /> Remember this is a world where you can actually attack or drive off the spirit of a knife, and then the knife won't cut. It's hard to do, but it shows that Gifts often have nothing at all to do with physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T04:22:24-07:00","id":860218,"title":"","content":"By that same logic, a door wouldn't open because you couldn't affect just the deabolt, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:10:11-07:00","id":860240,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;spirit of object&quot; wording is critical.<br /> Does every object have an individual spirit?<br /> Aren't most spirits supposed to be asleep?<br /> Does the gift only work on objects with awakened spirits or is it an instant Rite of Spirit Awakening? And possibly putting-back asleep effect?<br /> Does 'telling the spirit' involve actual speech ?<br /> Doesn't that require Spirit Speech, too ?<br /> Or is the gift meant to appeal to some general community of 'spirits of guns' somewhere in the Umbra who then help in doing what you want by means of magic?<br /> If the gift requires telling a spirit what you want, is it even applicable in a turn's time ?<br /> If the gift requires a spirit, does it fail if spirits aren't able to act on the scene in question, do to other gifts/fetish/etc effects that block their actions, but would not normally block gifts? And if so, why should the user of this gift be punished by some not that well thought out sentence the author wrote for this gift, but not the next?<br /> <br /> In general, I find the fluff of the gift is incompatible with most other spirit/umbra/gauntlet rules and therefore is ignored by me. And it is another example for WtA leaving a lot of stuff for the ST to rule because an author did write something that sounded fluffy, but didn't think it through and no editor made him change it later.<br /> <br /> I'd break it down to what the gift is supposed to do: Spend WP, roll dice to check if something happens, if so, affect a reasonably simple object in a way it is supposed to be affected. While the gift might be able to apply a relatively strong force to shift a lever, it might not be used to levitate an object with the same force, however.<br /> <br /> I often find it unnecessarily complicated to think to hard about how something works in the game world, since it is magic. I find it reasonable to figure out what a gift/fetish/Rite/etc. is supposed to accomplish in the game world and stick with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T09:28:47-07:00","id":860369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine?p=860188#post860188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me try and argue against the gift affecting guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>This line of reasoning ends with the Gift being the most useless Gift ever.<br /> <br /> If you don't allow the Gift to work on components of more complex machines by trying to force a specific interpretation of spirit-logic on the Gift instead of having spirit-logic serve the purpose of the Gift, it basically does nothing. The book's example of a light-switch is no different from a trigger or a keyboard key. It's a simple machine component of a larger system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T10:15:21-07:00","id":860401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine?p=860369#post860369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This line of reasoning ends with the Gift being the most useless Gift ever.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I disagree. It will stop being the most powerful level 1 gift (and probably level 2) to be an medium/low gift. Obviously, when controlled by a clever player.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T11:19:43-07:00","id":860447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine?p=860369#post860369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This line of reasoning ends with the Gift being the most useless Gift ever.<br /> <br /> If you don't allow the Gift to work on components of more complex machines by trying to force a specific interpretation of spirit-logic on the Gift instead of having spirit-logic serve the purpose of the Gift, it basically does nothing. The book's example of a light-switch is no different from a trigger or a keyboard key. It's a simple machine component of a larger system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> god, you're right, that is frustratingly fuzzy when they seem like they're so physically distinct. I mean, it seems like if you have a Gift for talking to more complex things, you could just compel the electrical system to turn on a light directly, without any switch involved, while a lightswitch would also be physically and conceptually distinct enough that it would also be workable...but yeah as a player the tiny distinctions could drive me up the wall if I wasn't super committed to the hyper-animist interpretation of everything, which I know not everyone is by a long shot.<br /> <br /> This is probably a case where I'd hold back as a player, and be careful if I was writing prose, but not kick up a fuss as an ST or if someone else was doing it.<br /> <br /> Still I think it's workable to open a door latch from the other side, or to drop a cargo container from a crane on someone by messing with the winch instead of the crane controls, and that kind of thing by itself makes me happy with the power level (per erSito).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:01:20-07:00","id":860507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine?p=860401#post860401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. It will stop being the most powerful level 1 gift (and probably level 2) to be an medium/low gift</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to hear the logic on this.<br /> <br /> 1) Its a Gift that's useless in the Umbra, and many of the deep wilderness areas the game deals with. Sure, it's a Glasswalker Gift and that means the ST should have more urban play where it is more useful, but it's inherently limited by devices even mattering to the situation. There's pretty much nothing it can do that you couldn't do with mundane skill or brute strength; it's main advantages are speed, stealth, and distance operation. If you're fighting a pack of BSDs away from human eyes so Crinos/Hispo are viable... what exactly is Control Simple Machine doing for you?<br /> <br /> 2) Let's see some comparisons to other Gifts. I'll start with a simple one: Persuasion. I'd love to see the argument that says Persuasion is a weaker Gift than Control Simple Machine.<br /> <br /> 3) How are you not making the Gift useless. Not just &quot;medium/low&quot; but flat out pointless. If you're using the spirit-of-the-item metric for the complexity of the systems you can impact, you can't even operate a freaking zipper with it, because a zipper is more complex than a single simple machine. What uses does it retain?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine?p=860447#post860447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">god, you're right, that is frustratingly fuzzy when they seem like they're so physically distinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>I go back to my first post. It's really not that fuzzy. You can operate a simple machine. If it is a component of a more complex system, you have zero direct control over the results of operating that simple machine. You can unlatch a window lock, but it isn't going to do anything about the security system on the window when you open it. You can pull the trigger of a gun, but you aren't aiming it with all the issues that entails as well as having to operate a safety separately (perhaps even no even with this Gift if a gun has an electronic safety). Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, it seems like if you have a Gift for talking to more complex things, you could just compel the electrical system to turn on a light directly, without any switch involved... </div> </div> </div>Well yeah. That's what Control Complex Machine is for, and does insanely more potent things. I mean... you can fly a helicopter without any skill at flying by using Control Complex Machine.<br /> <br /> If people feel Control Simple Machine is overpowered, I shudder to think about what you do with Control Complex Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T19:43:31-07:00","id":860730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/859682-what-is-a-simple-machine?p=860188#post860188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the description, it doesn't affect the physical object--it affects the spirit of the object, and that spirit causes the object to do something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this is an important part of the description. The Gift is affecting the entire machine/device. It is not a low level TK power that physically moves switches. Instead, you are telling the spirit to activate the machine/device. If the switch is part of a &quot;simple machine&quot; it works. If the switch is part of a &quot;complex machine&quot; it doesn't even though in both cases the activating mechanism is merely a switch.<br /> <br /> The examples given are extremely simple so I think it's best to err on the side of caution. This does make the gift less useful in modern chronicles because more and more machines in everyday use have become complicated devices. Many jobs that once used simple machines now use more complicated ones that serve the same function. That doesn't mean it is completely useless.<br /> <br /> I don't think it should apply to anything that has a simple triggering mechanism. I don't think it should activate assault rifles or turn on a house's electricity even though pulling a trigger or flipping a switch is easy. But we can't be making the machine so simple that we find almost no examples in the modern first world.<br /> <br /> I recommend to any ST that they come up with their own simple rules for guidance. Mine would be: no external power source, no electronics, no precision machinery required, nothing that cannot be classified in one of the six simple machines, and a limit to how how simple machines can be put together before it becomes &quot;complex&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't find Heavy Arm's arguments entirely without merit. Players are going to argue they want to use it to simply flip a light switch on, and not that they want a light bulb to turn on its own, even though the end result is the same. By itself, I would be fine with it. But I would be against the idea that a car should start simply because the turnkey should be moved. It is this kind of creeping logic that allows abuse. There are always going to hard cases, and hard cases make bad law. Personally, I find a harder assed approach easier to keep players' expectations in line and leads to less arguing than being initially easy going and needing to reel it in later.<br /> <br /> Most likely, if players want to make the distinction between the &quot;easy machine&quot; of a trigger or switch and the &quot;complex machine&quot; that provides the real effect, at this point I'd probably rule the light switch turns on, but the light does not. The trigger pulls, but no bullet comes out. I'd probably be OK with a simple bicycle, but not one that had many speed gears.<br /> <br /> Find your comfort zone and stick to it. There is not going to be unanimity on this, especially on every hard case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:22:46-07:00","id":860886,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of mentally chaffing at these continued assertions of &quot;abuse&quot; with no real elaboration on what's problematic with allowing the Gift to do various things. What does letting Control Simple Machine activate an electronic circuit via a physical switch allow that's problematic?<br /> <br /> There's this vague sense of a slippery slope to endless table debates/abuse/chaos... but no specificity of how we get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:31:44-07:00","id":860889,"title":"","content":"One of the most and memorable uses of control simple machines at my table involved the pulling of a trigger. The pistol in question was in the hands of a neighborhood watch volunteer who actually stopped the PCs and called the police when the officers arrived the player triggered the gun. The volunteer was discredited the PCs were renting a house in the area and walked away. <br /> While I have reservations about typing on a keyboard I have no problem with unlocking handcuffs, releasing a lever, dropping an external magazine, or pulling a trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:36:37-07:00","id":861101,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone's saying you can use Control Simple Machine to flat out type normally on a keyboard. I was arguing for it to allow a single keystroke as no different than flipping a light switch or squeezing a trigger. Trying to take over enough individual keys to type would be annoying enough to be inherently pointless in application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}